{"id": "EUVD-2026-82155", "enisaUuid": "f583c674-7312-3848-bf41-a8c66550317c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Reject arena frees below the arena base\n\nbpf_arena_free_pages() accepts scalar arena addresses. The runtime\nmasks the address to the low 32 bits and reconstructs a full user\naddress from the arena base before returning the range to the arena\nfree tree.\n\nWhen the scalar value is below the low 32 bits of the arena base,\nfull_uaddr falls below user_vm_start. The existing upper-end clipping\nthen turns this into an out-of-range free-tree offset. A later\nallocation can reuse that offset and return an address below the arena\nmapping.\n\nReject such frees before computing the clipped range.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:40", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/90453eaf8f14e7be0ab03983f2a93aeb6b990a58", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a968dffa5ab3c74d2ebb3a6233bf8b843f0bfc20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a08635656037aee9c12231ed384449c4ffb1a93", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5a71cb2db6d84ac0042549dcec266b18429d41e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93045", "GHSA-qfvw-mjm8-22x7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ec03acd-89e0-3c5a-95f4-3df989072775", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "12a37c1a-fc41-3c25-91bf-8828b049818d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "317460317a02a1af512697e6e964298dedd8a163 <8a08635656037aee9c12231ed384449c4ffb1a93"}, {"id": "4bd4e530-b761-3c32-8b93-ffc8206ae44f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "317460317a02a1af512697e6e964298dedd8a163 <90453eaf8f14e7be0ab03983f2a93aeb6b990a58"}, {"id": "59b85030-334d-357e-8459-42a92cc4654f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "61ee38b8-2ecc-39c9-b4e5-4b53433b773b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "317460317a02a1af512697e6e964298dedd8a163 <a968dffa5ab3c74d2ebb3a6233bf8b843f0bfc20"}, {"id": "68dc3327-3066-347e-8fc8-62bb6e352fb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "828a9550-f8ea-3e87-916c-d7a34da5b06f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "8bfa752d-4781-3aa0-bbac-a620a1fcc542", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "317460317a02a1af512697e6e964298dedd8a163 <b5a71cb2db6d84ac0042549dcec266b18429d41e"}, {"id": "8d33c7cd-67a3-3164-b08f-0a0af1802398", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "935ce301-80dc-34d5-aafc-733445eaca87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1a26884b-537f-3b4c-9e9b-1985dc9b9b7a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}